<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>To the Shores of Abu Musa, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;CMO: To the Shores of Abu Musa, 2021&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;The Time Is: 6 October 2021 20:00:00 Zulu/7 October 00:00:00 Abu Dubai Time&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Last Edited: 27 September 2020&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Abu Musa and Tunb Islands&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Playable as the U.S. - UAE Side&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;12 Hours Duration&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Thanks to AndrewJ and DWReese for their kind advice with this scenario! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Background: &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Long in dispute, on November 30, 1971 Shah Mohammad Reza Pahlavi’s Imperial Iranian Navy and Marines seized Abu Musa Island, Greater Tunb Island and Lesser Tunb Island pitting 2,000 Iranian Marines against 6 police officers. The results were inevitable but did cost three Iranian and four police officer’s lives. The United Arab Emirates (UAE) continued to dispute the Iranian occupation and claims.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On January 31st, 2019, the Commander of Iran's Revolutionary Guard Maj. Gen. Mohammad Ali Jafari said the three islands in the Gulf waters are an inalienable part of Iranian territory and that the armed forces will defend every inch of them without hesitation. Calling the islands, "the beating heart of Iran in the Persian Gulf," he threw down the gauntlet with the UAE and reignited the simmering dispute. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In May of 2020 the USS Pearl Harbor conducted amphibious exercises with UAE Army/Marine forces as the dispute continued to escalate. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In early October, 2021 tensions in the Arabian/Persian Gulf were especially high with the UAE and Iran trading accusations in the United Nations and International Court over Iranian Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps intercepts of tankers in the Gulf and Straits of Hormuz. This activity began after the USS Pearl Harbor arrived in the UAE for additional exercises on the 1st and the Amphibious Ready Group lead by the USS Iwo Jima (LHD-7) passed between Abu Musa and Greater Tunb Island on their way to a port call in Bahrain on the 2nd. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On October 3rd, encouraged by the American Administration the UAE demanded Iran withdraw all forces from the three islands, a demand quickly rejected by Iran. That afternoon multiple tankers were attacked by IRGC forces from all three islands including several owned by the UAE. Damage was light but one Ukrainian seaman was killed in the attacks.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The 4th brought continued tension in the Gulf with the USS Iwo Jima’s ARG setting sail for Abu Dubai under heavy escort. Additional IRGC Boghammer harassment of neutral shipping continued followed by an American ultimatum to cease all activities by midnight of October 6th. The UAE again pressed their case for the islands in the UN Security Council only to be vetoed by the PRC and Russia. American intelligence observed some additional readiness in the Bandar Abbas Region with Iranian aircraft gathering and increased readiness on the islands. Also vessels dropping objects into the water were videotaped by US Recon aircraft. In response TF 52.1 with three Avenger class MCMs and the USS Whidbey Island (LSD-41) with two MH-53E Sea Dragon MCM Helicopters and the four experimental Fleet Class CUSV [MCM] mine sweeping drones aboard were dispatched to the region from Manama, Bahrain.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The 5th was the day that convinced most shipping interests that　it was time to reduce their footprint in the Gulf. Many merchant skippers decided to wait to transit the disputed area with shipping stacking up in the Gulf of Oman. That was a good decision as by evening the 55,000 GT bulk cargo vessel "Mumbai Trader" was attacked and sunk with all hands lost. Reports were received that the crew radioed they were being machinegunned when they entered the water. India’s ambassador to Iran demanded answers but was rebuffed by the Foreign Ministry. The USN, USAF and UAE continued to increase readiness in the UAE as the remining Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) nations declared neutrality in the growing dispute. The U.S. announced their completed respect and adherence to that neutral position and that they would not utilize bases in Qatar, Saudi Arabia or Bahrain if military action proved necessary. USAF Aircraft based in those countries sent detachments to the UAE to support the 380th Air Expeditionary Wing basing at Al-Safran Ab, Al Dhafra AB and Al Minhad AB.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Dawn of October 6th saw two Iranian IRGC Cobra helicopter gunships orbiting the American flag Tanker M/V Liberty Bay southwest of Abu Musa. Calling for assistance, the USS Billings (LCS-15) was dispatched to her aid with some F-16CMs sortied for top cover, it was too late! At 07:16 a.m. the Iranians ordered the Liberty Bay to heave too for inspection which her master declined. After two more demands for her to stop the lead IRGC gunship raked the Bridge with her chain gun causing total carnage. The Ship’s Master, First Mate and Bos’un were immediately killed with several others mortally wounded. Missiles were then fired into the Engineering Decks by both gunships starting fires in her superstructure. Suddenly both helicopters veered away flying Nape Of The Earth (NOTE) back to Abu Musa, the F-16s were now in range. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the tense day demands and accusation flew between Abu Dhabi, Tehran, and Washington. The President and Emir of the UAE in a joint statement gave Iran until Sunrise 7 October to abandon the islands or they would be taken by force if necessary. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Billings and the Oceangoing Tug "Green Island" arrived on station with the Liberty Bay with F-16s flying CAP and a P-8A patrolling for any Iranian submarines. The fire was extinguished by midday and a tow line was shot to her which promptly parted. The Liberty Bay would have to make for Abu Dhabi under her own power and damage control and engineering crews from the Billings started the process to get her underway. The Green Island and Billings were tasked to escort her to safety.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;By 5 p.m. Iran had signaled their intentions to fight by attacking a Kuwaiti flag tanker off of Greater Tunb Island and American National Command Authority had authorized Central Command to seize the islands the next morning…&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NOTES:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;IMPORTANT: The game maps don’t line up well with the actual islands in the game (the BMNG and Land Cover maps come closest). I carefully rolled the cursor over the map surface and marked pure land areas with Reference Points (RPs). I used as many as 60 RPs to delineate land areas and the RPs do outline each of the three island areas land areas for amphibious operations. I locked those RPs and you should use them for your Amphibious/Cargo mission RPs. Bottom line is IGNORE the maps and use the RPs!!!!!! Also, you need those RPs to gain VPs for your amphibious operations so don’t delete them!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;U.S.-UAE units are worth many more VPs unit for unit. Why…&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;　　　　 1. You are the Americans and UAE so it’s your operation, your losses should hurt you more!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;　　　　 2. By and large UAE/U.S. equipment is much more expensive and each trooper represents a huge investment in resources.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;　　　　 3. Remember the USS Cole? Beirut Bombing? Americans by and large have a lower loss tolerance than many other nations. Loose high value units and many American lives and there will be Hell to pay in the American media, Congress and public opinion!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I have set up a few Missions at the beginning of the scenario. Since we are not at war, some are inactive (Al Minhad Air Intercept) and others are weapons tight. When the fighting actually begins you might want to change their ROE (Heck you might want to change their ROE early but it may result in the opening of hostilities before you are ready). I have added a No Navigation Zone for the U.S.-UAE Player side, really to keep the AI from racing over Iran when a real pilot wouldn't in this situation. You can still attack the coastal areas.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I really tried to keep this scenario under control! Those who have played my scenarios know I cover all bases (too many to be honest). This time I stopped! No THAADS, No IRBM/SRBMs, No Qatar or Saudi Bases! These are deliberate decisions. I could have gone nuts here (and have before!).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is my first attempt at both　Combat Cargo Missions and Mine Missions. I hope you enjoy it! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01, Build 1147.11 &lt;FONT size=3 face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face="Courier New"&gt;– Data Base: DB3000 487&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face="Courier New"&gt;Rebuilt 10/16/2020 under CMO Version V1.02, Build 1147.13 - Data base: DB3000 487&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Both .INI and .Delta files have been provided for deep rebuilds&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
